<#
.SYNOPSIS
    Exports what the MSWPO SPFx rebuild needs from SharePoint that is not in the source export (READ-ONLY).

.DESCRIPTION
    Nothing in SharePoint is created, changed or deleted. Output (under -OutDir, default ..\docs):
      schemas\<list>.json            list settings + every field (internal name, title, type, required, choices, SchemaXml),
                                     NewForm/EditForm/DispForm JSLink values, classic workflow associations
      schemas\_index.json            one line per list (found/missing, item count, field count, workflows)
      legacy-ui\pages\<page>.*       Site Pages wiki HTML (WikiField) and each web part's XML (Script/Content Editor code)
      legacy-ui\site-assets.csv      inventory of SiteAssets/MSWPO on the site
      legacy-ui\site-assets-missing\ files present in SiteAssets/MSWPO but missing from the local MSWPO\ export
      legacy-ui\access-groups.json   group names (Title) from MSWPO Access Management + member count (no member names)

.REQUIREMENTS
    - PowerShell 7.2+  (pwsh)
    - PnP.PowerShell 2.x or later:  Install-Module PnP.PowerShell -Scope CurrentUser
    - An Entra ID app registration for PnP interactive sign-in (the shared PnP app was retired in 2024):
          Register-PnPEntraIDAppForInteractiveLogin -ApplicationName "PnP MSWPO export" -Tenant arlingtonva.onmicrosoft.com
      (needs SharePoint delegated permissions; an admin may have to grant consent) - pass its Client ID below.
    - Account with Read access to /sites/wpcb/mswpo, /sites/wpcb/ops and /sites/wpcb/lab.

.EXAMPLE
    pwsh ./tools/Export-MswpoSchema.ps1 -ClientId 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
#>
